{"1-5":{"people":[{"id":"achan-h5912","name":"Achan","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Carmi","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"carmi-h3756h","name":"Carmi","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Zabdi","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"zabdi-h2067g","name":"Zabdi","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Zerah","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"zerah-h2226i","name":"Zerah","kind":"person","brief":"Judah's son","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"joshua-h3091g","name":"Joshua","kind":"person","brief":"A judge","count":2,"firstVerse":2}],"places":[{"id":"ai-h5857g","name":"Ai","kind":"place","brief":"","count":4,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"beth-aven-h1007","name":"Beth-aven","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"bethel-h1008g","name":"Bethel","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"jericho-h3405g","name":"Jericho","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"shebarim-h7671","name":"Shebarim","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":5}],"words":[{"base":"H5857","lemma":"עַי","tr":"ay","gloss":"Ai","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":40},{"base":"H5927","lemma":"עָלָה","tr":"a·lah","gloss":"to ascend: rise","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":889},{"base":"H0582","lemma":"אֱנוֹשׁ","tr":"e·nosh","gloss":"human","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":565},{"base":"H1007","lemma":"בֵּית אָ֫וֶן","tr":"bet a·ven","gloss":"Beth-aven","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":14},{"base":"H7270","lemma":"רָגַל","tr":"ra·gal","gloss":"to spy","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":25},{"base":"H2764","lemma":"חֵ֫רֶם","tr":"che·rem","gloss":"devoted thing","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":38},{"base":"H5221","lemma":"נָכָה","tr":"na·khah","gloss":"to smite","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":500},{"base":"H0505","lemma":"אֶ֫לֶף","tr":"e·leph","gloss":"thousand","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":506},{"base":"H1008","lemma":"בֵּֽיתְ־אֵל","tr":"bet-el","gloss":"Bethel","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":142},{"base":"H3091","lemma":"יְהוֹשׁוּעַ","tr":"ye·ho·shu·a","gloss":"Joshua","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":218}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JOS","chapter":22,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"Was not Achan son of Zerah unfaithful regarding what was set apart for destruction, bringing wrath upon the whole congregation of Israel? Yet it was not only Achan who perished because of his sin!’”","from":1},{"book":"DEU","chapter":28,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"The LORD will cause you to be defeated before your enemies. You will march out against them in one direction but flee from them in seven. You will be an object of horror to all the kingdoms of the earth.","from":4},{"book":"JOS","chapter":18,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"On the north side their border began at the Jordan, went up past the northern slope of Jericho, headed west through the hill country, and came out at the wilderness of Beth-aven.","from":2},{"book":"1CH","chapter":2,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"The sons of Zerah: Zimri, Ethan, Heman, Calcol, and Dara—five in all.","from":1},{"book":"1CH","chapter":2,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"The son of Carmi: Achar, who brought trouble upon Israel by violating the ban on devoted things.","from":1},{"book":"ECC","chapter":9,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Wisdom is better than weapons of war, but one sinner destroys much good.","from":1},{"book":"LEV","chapter":26,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"And I will set My face against you, so that you will be defeated by your enemies. Those who hate you will rule over you, and you will flee when no one pursues you.","from":4},{"book":"JOS","chapter":2,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"and said to them, “I know that the LORD has given you this land and that the fear of you has fallen on us, so that all who dwell in the land are melting in fear of you.","from":5}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"6-9":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":2,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"joshua-h3091g","name":"Joshua","kind":"person","brief":"A judge","count":2,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"amorites-h0567","name":"Amorites","kind":"person","brief":"Canaanites","count":1,"firstVerse":7}],"places":[{"id":"jordan-h3383","name":"Jordan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"canaan-h3667a","name":"Canaan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":9}],"words":[{"base":"H4100","lemma":"מָה","tr":"mah","gloss":"what?","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":752},{"base":"H3383","lemma":"יַרְדֵּן","tr":"yar·den","gloss":"Jordan","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":182},{"base":"H3091","lemma":"יְהוֹשׁוּעַ","tr":"ye·ho·shu·a","gloss":"Joshua","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":218},{"base":"H0136","lemma":"אֲדֹנָי","tr":"a·do·nai","gloss":"Lord","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":440},{"base":"H5674","lemma":"עָבַר","tr":"a·var","gloss":"to pass","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":556},{"base":"H0994","lemma":"בִּי","tr":"bi","gloss":"please","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":12},{"base":"H8034","lemma":"שֵׁם","tr":"shem","gloss":"name","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":864},{"base":"H0162","lemma":"אֲהָהּ","tr":"a·hah","gloss":"alas!","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":15},{"base":"H2974","lemma":"יָאַל","tr":"ya·al","gloss":"be willing","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":19},{"base":"H3427","lemma":"יָשַׁב","tr":"ya·shav","gloss":"to dwell","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":1079}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":37,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"When Reuben returned to the pit and saw that Joseph was not there, he tore his clothes,","from":6},{"book":"EXO","chapter":32,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Why should the Egyptians declare, ‘He brought them out with evil intent, to kill them in the mountains and wipe them from the face of the earth’? Turn from Your fierce anger and relent from doing harm to Your people.","from":9},{"book":"GEN","chapter":37,"verse":34,"verseEnd":34,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Then Jacob tore his clothes, put sackcloth around his waist, and mourned for his son many days.","from":6},{"book":"PSA","chapter":83,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"saying, “Come, let us erase them as a nation; may the name of Israel be remembered no more.”","from":9},{"book":"EZK","chapter":36,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"Therefore tell the house of Israel that this is what the Lord GOD says: It is not for your sake that I will act, O house of Israel, but for My holy name, which you profaned among the nations to which you went.","from":9},{"book":"EZK","chapter":36,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"I will show the holiness of My great name, which has been profaned among the nations—the name you have profaned among them. Then the nations will know that I am the LORD, declares the Lord GOD, when I show My holiness in you before their eyes.","from":9},{"book":"ROM","chapter":3,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"But if our unrighteousness highlights the righteousness of God, what shall we say? That God is unjust to inflict His wrath on us? I am speaking in human terms.","from":8},{"book":"ROM","chapter":3,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"Certainly not! In that case, how could God judge the world?","from":8}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"10-15":{"people":[{"id":"joshua-h3091g","name":"Joshua","kind":"person","brief":"A judge","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":4,"firstVerse":11}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H2764","lemma":"חֵ֫רֶם","tr":"che·rem","gloss":"devoted thing","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":38},{"base":"H3920","lemma":"לָכַד","tr":"la·khad","gloss":"to capture","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":121},{"base":"H1571","lemma":"גַּם","tr":"gam","gloss":"also","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":769},{"base":"H7126","lemma":"קָרַב","tr":"qa·rav","gloss":"to present: come","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":280},{"base":"H6965","lemma":"קָמָי","tr":"qa·may","gloss":"(Leb)-kamai","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":628},{"base":"H7130","lemma":"קֶ֫רֶב","tr":"qe·rev","gloss":"entrails: among","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":227},{"base":"H0341","lemma":"אֹיֵב","tr":"o·yev","gloss":"enemy","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":282},{"base":"H6942","lemma":"קָדַשׁ","tr":"qa·dash","gloss":"to consecrate: consecate","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":171},{"base":"H7626","lemma":"שֵׁ֫בֶט","tr":"she·vet","gloss":"tribe: staff","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":190},{"base":"H3201","lemma":"יָכֹל","tr":"ya·khol","gloss":"be able","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":194}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"LAM","chapter":3,"verse":40,"verseEnd":40,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"Let us examine and test our ways, and turn back to the LORD.","from":13},{"book":"LAM","chapter":3,"verse":41,"verseEnd":41,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"Let us lift up our hearts and hands to God in heaven:","from":13},{"book":"JOS","chapter":3,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Then Joshua told the people, “Consecrate yourselves, for tomorrow the LORD will do wonders among you.”","from":13},{"book":"PSA","chapter":5,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"For You are not a God who delights in wickedness; no evil can dwell with You.","from":12},{"book":"PSA","chapter":5,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"The boastful cannot stand in Your presence; You hate all workers of iniquity.","from":12},{"book":"ACT","chapter":5,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"Now a man named Ananias, together with his wife Sapphira, also sold a piece of property.","from":11},{"book":"ACT","chapter":5,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"With his wifeʼs full knowledge, he kept back some of the proceeds for himself, but brought a portion and laid it at the apostlesʼ feet.","from":11},{"book":"GEN","chapter":34,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"When Jacobʼs sons heard what had happened, they returned from the field. They were filled with grief and fury, because Shechem had committed an outrage in Israel by lying with Jacobʼs daughter—a thing that should not be done.","from":15}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"16-26":{"people":[{"id":"joshua-h3091g","name":"Joshua","kind":"person","brief":"A judge","count":7,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":6,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":3,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"zerah-h2226i","name":"Zerah","kind":"person","brief":"Judah's son","count":3,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"zabdi-h2067g","name":"Zabdi","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Zerah","count":2,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"achan-h5912","name":"Achan","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Carmi","count":4,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"carmi-h3756h","name":"Carmi","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Zabdi","count":1,"firstVerse":18}],"places":[{"id":"shinar-h8152","name":"Shinar","kind":"place","brief":"In Mesopotamia","count":1,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"achor-valley-h5911","name":"Achor Valley","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":24}],"words":[{"base":"H3091","lemma":"יְהוֹשׁוּעַ","tr":"ye·ho·shu·a","gloss":"Joshua","lang":"h","inPassage":7,"uses":218},{"base":"H5912","lemma":"עָכָן","tr":"a·khan","gloss":"Achan","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":6},{"base":"H0168","lemma":"אֹ֫הֶל","tr":"o·hel","gloss":"tent","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":345},{"base":"H3920","lemma":"לָכַד","tr":"la·khad","gloss":"to capture","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":121},{"base":"H7126","lemma":"קָרַב","tr":"qa·rav","gloss":"to present: come","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":280},{"base":"H3701","lemma":"כֶּ֫סֶף","tr":"ke·seph","gloss":"silver: money","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":403},{"base":"H5911","lemma":"עָכוֹר","tr":"a·khor","gloss":"(Valley of) Achor","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":5},{"base":"H2067","lemma":"זַבְדִּי","tr":"zav·di","gloss":"Zabdi","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":6},{"base":"H2227","lemma":"זַרְחִי","tr":"zar·chi","gloss":"Zerahite","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":6},{"base":"H0155","lemma":"אַדֶּ֫רֶת","tr":"ad·de·ret","gloss":"clothing","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":12}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1SA","chapter":6,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Make images of your tumors and of the rats that are ravaging the land. Give glory to the God of Israel, and perhaps He will lift His hand from you and your gods and your land.","from":19},{"book":"JOS","chapter":6,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"But keep away from the things devoted to destruction, lest you yourself be set apart for destruction. If you take any of these, you will set apart the camp of Israel for destruction and bring disaster upon it.","from":25},{"book":"JER","chapter":13,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Give glory to the LORD your God before He brings darkness, before your feet stumble on the dusky mountains. You wait for light, but He turns it into deep gloom and thick darkness.","from":19},{"book":"JHN","chapter":9,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"So a second time they called for the man who had been blind and said, “Give glory to God! We know that this man is a sinner.”","from":19},{"book":"JAS","chapter":1,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Then after desire has conceived, it gives birth to sin; and sin, when it is full-grown, gives birth to death.","from":21},{"book":"NUM","chapter":26,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"These were the descendants of Judah by their clans: The Shelanite clan from Shelah, the Perezite clan from Perez, and the Zerahite clan from Zerah.","from":17},{"book":"1CH","chapter":2,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"The son of Carmi: Achar, who brought trouble upon Israel by violating the ban on devoted things.","from":25},{"book":"PSA","chapter":119,"verse":37,"verseEnd":37,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Turn my eyes away from worthless things; revive me with Your word.","from":21}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]}}